Adaptation by Chen Gao, 2026:
- Native Typst layout replaces the LaTeX implementation.
- EB Garamond and Garamond-Math are the default fonts from version 0.2.0.
- Libertinus Serif and New Computer Modern Math remain selectable alternatives.
- Modern spelling, standard ligatures, and lining numerals replace the
  historical demonstration treatment; tables use tabular numerals.
- Headings, research-memo metadata, and a height-reserving margin-note block
  are added. The starter enables a three-line drop capital from droplet.
  Engraved figures remain outside the scope of this memo template.
- Version 0.3.0 adds independently drawn native vector torn-paper emphasis
  blocks with shadows and varied, deterministic tape placement. No image assets
  or additional package dependencies are introduced.
- Version 0.4.0 adds tiled vector paper fibers, a darker page edge, running
  heads, captions above tables, and block-quotation styling.
- The English starter reproduces F. Galton, "Vox Populi," Nature 75 (1907),
  450-451, and the Chinese example reproduces Shen Kuo's 隙积术 from 梦溪笔谈,
  volume 18; both texts are in the public domain. Headings, notes, and layout
  were added independently.
- Chinese mode adds ChillKai handwriting, localized labels, paragraph indentation,
  upright headings, 0.020 em outlined titles and strong text, and underlined
  emphasis. Font files are not modified. Source Han Serif SC is a selectable
  printed-book alternative. Both fonts are external OFL-1.1 requirements;
  no font files are distributed.

No upstream demonstration prose, figures, font binaries, MetaPost, or fiziko
code is distributed in this package. fiziko is a separate GPL-3.0 work and is
not a dependency of sepia-memo.

